ent"}],"error":{},"testCase":{"id":"12c56e53a7b1a42546b824de5cebb73d","externalId":"d33054d241b0cc11de9bf3b28d6eda47","name":"summarize_retaliations writes a queryable [retaliation]-tagged memory for the retaliating NPC (KER-12)","fullName":"tests.test_director_dialogue_memory.TestDialogueHandlerLongTermMemory#test_summarize_retaliations_creates_queryable_memory"},"descriptionHtml":"<p>Regression for KER-12.</p>\n<pre><code>    Without this pass, ``check_retaliation`` fires an Actor call for a\n    bystander NPC whose mood flipped, appends the response to the\n    turn's dialogue output, and moves on — no graph memory is created.\n    On the next encounter ``get_memories_held_by(retaliator)`` returns\n    nothing about the fight. This test wires the new\n    ``DialogueHandler.summarize_retaliations`` to a real\n    ``MemoryManager`` and asserts both (a) the memory exists in the\n    graph and (b) the summariser saw a ``[retaliation]``-prefixed log\n    so downstream prompts can distinguish provoked combat from\n    targeted combat.\n</code></pre>\n","environment":"default","setup":[{"id":"957916099c847162037fd3a7120195b6","type":"before","name":"_install_log_scrubber","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"f08d6f3f05793fab1f5afe9a6cb34784","type":"before","name":"_function_scoped_runner","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"ece548debc05cf7dc5ffcc869786e208","type":"before","name":"event_loop_policy","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"teardown":[{"id":"b594100aec865aaea342960789d7f1de","type":"after","name":"_install_log_scrubber::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"7053a15bcc7134dda63d835f82e5577f","type":"after","name":"_function_scoped_runner::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["tests","test_director_dialogue_memory","TestDialogueHandlerLongTermMemory"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":["tests","test_director_dialogue_memory.py","TestDialogueHandlerLongTermMemory"],"